From: K230 AMP development <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: k230: describe small-core AMP slot on CanMV-K230 V3

Same AMP carveout as the CanMV-K230 board, applied to the V3 device tree.
k230-canmv-v3.dts includes k230.dtsi directly rather than the CanMV board DTS,
so the reservation and the UART3 handover have to be repeated here; the ISA and
mailbox changes in k230.dtsi are shared and are not duplicated.

The carveout keeps the same physical addresses as the 512 MiB CanMV board even
though V3 declares 1 GiB of RAM, so one big-core firmware binary and one set of
driver constants serve both boards. On V3 this is a hole in the middle of RAM
rather than the top 64 MiB; Linux keeps everything above it.

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-v3.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/k230-canmv-v3.dts
@@ -27,6 +27,22 @@
 		reg = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x40000000>;
 	};
 
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+
+		big_core_firmware: big-core-firmware@1c000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x1c000000 0x0 0x01000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		amp_shared_memory: amp-shared-memory@1d000000 {
+			reg = <0x0 0x1d000000 0x0 0x03000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+	};
+
 	sound {
 		status                      = "okay";
 		compatible                  = "canaan,k230-audio-inno";
@@ -39,8 +55,9 @@
 &uart0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+/* UART3 is connected to CH342 channel B and belongs to big-core firmware. */
 &uart3 {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 &mmc_sd1{
 	status = "okay";
